// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING:
// New Zealand is a CONFIDENT market with one of the cleanest
// homeschool frameworks in the English-speaking world (Education and
// Training Act 2020, s.38):
// - Home education runs on a per-child CERTIFICATE OF EXEMPTION from
//   the Ministry of Education. Free application to the local MoE
//   office, typical processing 4-6 weeks. The legal test is a
//   quality-of-provision standard — the child "is to be taught at
//   least as regularly and well as in a registered school" — NOT a
//   curriculum mandate. No mandatory curriculum, no testing, no
//   parental qualification requirement.
// - Compulsory schooling ages 6-16. The exemption runs until 16 or
//   school enrolment; education after 16 is simply not compulsory.
//   The child must remain enrolled until the exemption is granted.
// - Twice-yearly declaration (around April and October) is a legal
//   obligation; failure may trigger an Education Review Office
//   review. The declaration also elects the allowance:
// - THE HOME EDUCATION SUPERVISION ALLOWANCE — the state PAYS
//   home-educating families: approximately NZD 770-800/year for the
//   first child, declining for siblings, paid twice yearly. Almost
//   no other country does this. Around 10,800 students were
//   registered home-educated in 2024.
// - HONEST 2026 NOTE — include wherever the framework is described:
//   in May 2026 the Education Minister announced that the Education
//   and Training (System Reform) Amendment Bill will incorporate new
//   checks on home-educating parents. The framework remains
//   exemption-based; families should follow Ministry guidance as the
//   reform lands, and our documentation-first approach is built for
//   exactly that direction of travel.
//
// THE DISTINCTIVE NZ WEDGE: New Zealand's own leading schools chose
// Cambridge — Auckland Grammar, Macleans College, the ACG network and
// others run CAIE alongside or instead of NCEA — so Cambridge exam
// infrastructure is genuinely deep, private-candidate sittings are
// established practice, and NZQA recognises A-Levels and the IB for
// University Entrance. We are not importing a foreign curriculum;
// we are teaching the one NZ's top schools already picked.
//
// TIMEZONE — THE USUAL FRAMING FLIPS. New Zealand runs NZST (UTC+12)
// / NZDT (UTC+13) — 9-10 HOURS AHEAD of Nairobi EAT. The honest
// framing: live teaching in the Nairobi MORNING lands in the New
